H2400.definition:
intensively from H2398 (חָטָא);
a criminal, or one accounted guilty
KJV: offender, sinful, sinner.

H2401.definition:
feminine of H2399 (חֵטְא);
an offence, or a sacrifice forit
KJV: sin (offering).

H2402.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H2401 (חֲטָאָה);
an offence, and the penalty or sacrifice forit
KJV: sin (offering).

H2403.definition:
or חַטָּאת; from H2398 (חָטָא);
an offence (sometimes habitual sinfulness), and its penalty, occasion, sacrifice, or expiation; also (concretely) an offender
KJV: punishment (of sin), purifying(-fication for sin), sin(-ner, offering).

H2404.definition:
a primitive root;
to chop or carve wood
KJV: cut down, hew(-er), polish.

H2405.definition:
feminine passive participle of H2404 (חָטַב);
properly, a carving; hence, a tapestry (as figured)
KJV: carved.

H2406.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
wheat, whether the grain or the plant
KJV: wheat(-en).

H2407.definition:
from an unused root of uncertain signification;
Chattush, the name of four or five Israelites
KJV: Hattush.

H2408.definition:
(Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H2398 (חָטָא);
an offence
KJV: sin.

H2409.definition:
(Aramaic) from the same as H2408 (חֲטִי);
an expiation
KJV: sin offering.

H2410.definition:
from an unused root apparently meaning to dig out; explorer;
Chatita, a temple porter
KJV: Hatita.

H2411.definition:
from an unused root apparently meaning to wave; fluctuating;
Chattil, one of 'Solomon's servants'
KJV: Hattil.

H2412.definition:
from H2414 (חָטַף); robber;
Chatipha, one of the Nethinim
KJV: Hatipha.

H2413.definition:
a primitive root;
to stop
KJV: refrain.

H2414.definition:
a primitive root;
to clutch; hence, to seize as aprisoner
KJV: catch.

H2415.definition:
from an unused root of uncertain signification;
a twig
KJV: rod.

H2416.definition:
from H2421 (חָיָה);
alive; hence, raw (flesh); fresh (plant, water, year), strong; also (as noun, especially in the feminine singular and masculine plural) life (or living thing), whether literally or figuratively
KJV: [phrase] age, alive, appetite, (wild) beast, company, congregation, life(-time), live(-ly), living (creature, thing), maintenance, [phrase] merry, multitude, [phrase] (be) old, quick, raw, running, springing, troop.

H2417.definition:
(Aramaic) from H2418 (חֲיָא);
alive; also (as noun in plural) life
KJV: life, that liveth, living.

H2418.definition:
(Aramaic) or חֲיָה; (Aramaic), corresponding to H2421 (חָיָה);
to live
KJV: live, keep alive.

H2419.definition:
from H2416 (חַי) and H410 (אֵל); living of God;
Chiel, an Israelite
KJV: Hiel.

H2420.definition:
from H2330 (חוּד);
a puzzle, hence, a trick, conundrum, sententious maxim
KJV: dark saying (sentence, speech), hard question, proverb, riddle.

H2421.definition:
a primitive root (compare H2331 (חָוָה), H2421 (חָיָה));
to live, whether literally or figuratively; causatively, to revive
KJV: keep (leave, make) alive, [idiom] certainly, give (promise) life, (let, suffer to) live, nourish up, preserve (alive), quicken, recover, repair, restore (to life), revive, ([idiom] God) save (alive, life, lives), [idiom] surely, be whole.

H2423.definition:
(Aramaic) from H2418 (חֲיָא);
an animal
KJV: beast.

H2425.definition:
a primitive root (compare H2421 (חָיָה));
to live; causatively to revive
KJV: live, save life.

H2426.definition:
or (shortened) חֵל; a collateral form of H2428 (חַיִל);
an army; also (by analogy,) an intrenchment
KJV: army, bulwark, host, [phrase] poor, rampart, trench, wall.

H2427.definition:
and (feminine) חִילָה; from H2342 (חוּל);
a throe (expectant of childbirth)
KJV: pain, pang, sorrow.

H2428.definition:
from H2342 (חוּל);
probably a force, whether of men, means or other resources; an army, wealth, virtue, valor, strength
KJV: able, activity, ([phrase]) army, band of men (soldiers), company, (great) forces, goods, host, might, power, riches, strength, strong, substance, train, ([phrase]) valiant(-ly), valour, virtuous(-ly), war, worthy(-ily).

H2429.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H2428 (חַיִל);
an army, or strength
KJV: aloud, army, [idiom] most (mighty), power.

H2430.definition:
feminine of H2428 (חַיִל);
an intrenchment
KJV: bulwark.

H2431.definition:
or חֵלָאםxlit Chêlʼâm corrected to Chêlâʼm; from H2428 (חַיִל); fortress;
Chelam, a place East of Palestine
KJV: Helam.

H2432.definition:
from H2428 (חַיִל); fortress;
Chilen, a place in Palestine
KJV: Hilen.

H2433.definition:
another form for H2580 (חֵן);
beauty
KJV: comely.

H2434.definition:
another form for H2351 (חוּץ);
a wall
KJV: wall.

H2435.definition:
from H2434 (חַיִץ);
properly, the (outer) wall side; hence, exterior; figuratively, secular (as opposed to sacred)
KJV: outer, outward, utter, without.

H2436.definition:
or חֵק; and חוֹק; from an unused root, apparently meaning to inclose;
the bosom (literally or figuratively)
KJV: bosom, bottom, lap, midst, within.

H2437.definition:
from H2357 (חָוַר) in the sense of splendor;
Chirah, an Adullamite
KJV: Hirah.

H2438.definition:
or חִירוֹםlemma חִירֹם missing vav, corrected to חִירוֹם; another form of H2361 (חוּרָם);
Chiram or Chirom, the name of two Tyrians
KJV: Hiram, Huram.

H2439.definition:
another form of H2363 (חוּשׁ);
to hurry
KJV: make haste.

H2440.definition:
from H2439 (חִישׁ);
properly, a hurry; hence (adverb) quickly
KJV: soon.

H2441.definition:
probably from H2596 (חָנַךְ) in the sense of tasting;
properly, the palate or inside of the mouth; hence, the mouth itself (as the organ of speech, taste and kissing)
KJV: (roof of the) mouth, taste.

H2442.definition:
a primitive root (apparently akin to H2707 (חָקָה) through the idea of piercing);
properly, to adhere to; hence, to await
KJV: long, tarry, wait.

H2443.definition:
probably from H2442 (חָכָה);
a hook (as adhering)
KJV: angle, hook.

H2444.definition:
from the same as H2447 (חַכְלִיל); dark;
Chakilah, a hill in Palestine
KJV: Hachilah.

H2445.definition:
(Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H2449 (חָכַם);
wise, i.e. a Magian
KJV: wise.

H2446.definition:
from the base of H2447 (חַכְלִיל) and H3050 (יָהּ); darkness of Jah;
Chakaljah, an Israelite
KJV: Hachaliah.

H2447.definition:
by reduplication from an unused root apparently meaning to be dark;
darkly flashing (only of the eyes); in a good sense, brilliant (as stimulated by wine)
KJV: red.

H2448.definition:
from H2447 (חַכְלִיל);
flash (of the eyes); in a bad sense, blearedness
KJV: redness.

H2450.definition:
from H2449 (חָכַם);
wise, (i.e. intelligent, skilful or artful)
KJV: cunning (man), subtil, (un-), wise((hearted), man).

H2451.definition:
from H2449 (חָכַם);
wisdom (in a good sense)
KJV: skilful, wisdom, wisely, wit.

H2452.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H2451 (חׇכְמָה);
wisdom
KJV: wisdom.

H2453.definition:
from H2449 (חָכַם); skilful;
Chakmoni, an Israelite
KJV: Hachmoni, Hachmonite.

H2454.definition:
or חַכְמוֹת; collateral forms of H2451 (חׇכְמָה);
wisdom
KJV: wisdom, every wise (woman).

H2455.definition:
from H2490 (חָלַל);
properly, exposed; hence, profane
KJV: common, profane (place), unholy.

H2456.definition:
a primitive root (compare H2470 (חָלָה));
to be sick
KJV: be diseased.

H2457.definition:
from H2456 (חָלָא);
properly, disease; hence, rust
KJV: scum.

H2458.definition:
the same as H2457 (חֶלְאָה);
Chelah, an Israelitess
KJV: Helah.

H2459.definition:
or חֵלֶב; from an unused root meaning to be fat;
fat, whether literally or figuratively; hence, the richest or choice part
KJV: [idiom] best, fat(-ness), [idiom] finest, grease, marrow.

H2460.definition:
the same as H2459 (חֶלֶב); fatness;
Cheleb, an Israelite
KJV: Heleb.

H2461.definition:
from the same as H2459 (חֶלֶב);
milk (as the richness of kine)
KJV: [phrase] cheese, milk, sucking.

H2462.definition:
feminine of H2459 (חֶלֶב); fertility;
Chelbah, a place in Palestine
KJV: Helbah.

H2463.definition:
from H2459 (חֶלֶב); fruitful;
Chelbon, a place in Syria
KJV: Helbah.

H2464.definition:
from H2459 (חֶלֶב);
galbanam, an odorous gum (as if fatty)
KJV: galbanum.

H2465.definition:
from an unused root apparently meaning to glide swiftly;
life (as a fleeting portion of time); hence, the world (as transient)
KJV: age, short time, world.

H2466.definition:
the same as H2465 (חֶלֶד);
Cheled, an Israelite
KJV: Heled.

H2467.definition:
from the same as H2465 (חֶלֶד);
a weasel (from its gliding motion)
KJV: weasel.

H2468.definition:
feminine of H2467 (חֹלֶד);
Chuldah, an Israelitess
KJV: Huldah.

H2469.definition:
from H2466 (חֵלֶד); worldliness;
Cheldai, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Heldai.

H2470.definition:
a primitive root (compare H2342 (חוּל), H2470 (חָלָה), H2490 (חָלַל));
properly, to be rubbed or worn; hence (figuratively) to be weak, sick, afflicted; or (causatively) to grieve, make sick; also to stroke (in flattering), entreat
KJV: beseech, (be) diseased, (put to) grief, be grieved, (be) grievous, infirmity, intreat, lay to, put to pain, [idiom] pray, make prayer, be (fall, make) sick, sore, be sorry, make suit ([idiom] supplication), woman in travail, be (become) weak, be wounded.

H2471.definition:
from H2490 (חָלַל);
a cake (as usually punctured)
KJV: cake.

H2472.definition:
or (shortened) חֲלֹם; from H2492 (חָלַם);
a dream
KJV: dream(-er).

H2473.definition:
or (shortened) חֹלֹן; probably from H2344 (חוֹל); sandy;
Cholon, the name of two places in Palestine
KJV: Holon.

H2475.definition:
from H2498 (חָלַף);
properly, surviving; by implication (collectively) orphans
KJV: [idiom] destruction.

H2476.definition:
feminine passive participle of H2522 (חָלַשׁ);
defeat
KJV: being overcome.

H2477.definition:
probably of foreign origin;
Chalach, a region of Assyria
KJV: Halah.

H2478.definition:
by reduplication from H2342 (חוּל); contorted;
Chalchul, a place in Palestine
KJV: Halhul.

H2479.definition:
feminine from the same as H2478 (חַלְחוּל);
writhing (in childbirth); by implication, terror
KJV: (great, much) pain.

H2480.definition:
a primitive root;
to snatch at
KJV: catch.

H2481.definition:
from H2470 (חָלָה);
a trinket (as polished)
KJV: jewel, ornament.

H2482.definition:
the same as H2481 (חֲלִי);
Chali, a place in Palestine
KJV: Hali.

H2483.definition:
from H2470 (חָלָה);
malady, anxiety, calamity
KJV: disease, grief, (is) sick(-ness).

H2484.definition:
feminine of H2481 (חֲלִי);
a trinket
KJV: jewel.

H2485.definition:
from H2490 (חָלַל);
a flute (as perforated)
KJV: pipe.

H2486.definition:
or חָלִלָה; a directive from H2490 (חָלַל);
literal fora profaned thing; used (interj.) far be it!
KJV: be far, ([idiom] God) forbid.

H2487.definition:
from H2498 (חָלַף);
alternation
KJV: change, course.

H2489.definition:
or חֵלְכָה; apparently from an unused root probably meaning to be dark or (figuratively) unhappy;
a wretch, i.e. unfortunate
KJV: poor.

H2491.definition:
from H2490 (חָלַל);
pierced (especially to death); figuratively, polluted
KJV: kill, profane, slain (man), [idiom] slew, (deadly) wounded.

H2492.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to bind firmly, i.e. (by implication) to be (causatively to make) plump; also (through the figurative sense of dumbness) to dream
KJV: (cause to) dream(-er), be in good liking, recover.

H2493.definition:
(Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H2492 (חָלַם);
a dream
KJV: dream.

H2494.definition:
from H2492 (חָלַם); a dream;
Chelem, an Israelite
KJV: Helem. Compare H2469 (חֶלְדַּי).

H2495.definition:
from H2492 (חָלַם) (in the sense of insipidity);
probably purslain
KJV: egg.

H2496.definition:
probably from H2492 (חָלַם) (in the sense of hardness);
flint
KJV: flint(-y), rock.

H2497.definition:
from H2428 (חַיִל); strong;
Chelon, an Israelite
KJV: Helon.

H2498.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to slide by, i.e. (by implication) to hasten away, pass on, spring up, pierce or change
KJV: abolish, alter, change, cut off, go on forward, grow up, be over, pass (away, on, through), renew, sprout, strike through.

H2499.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H2498 (חָלַף);
to pass on (of time)
KJV: pass.
